      "problem": "There is some pair of real numbers such that the difference of their squares is equal to double their sum.\n\nExpress the statement above in formal language.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The words \"there is\" indicate that we use an existential quantifier, $∃.$\n\n- The sentence refers to two real numbers. So, by denoting our numbers as $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n∃\\,x,y\\in R.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=2(x+y)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows:\n\n$∃\\,x,y\\in R,\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=2(x+y)$",
